SUMMARY:Pollinator Meadow Volunteer Workday
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\nCome close
  out 2026 at the Pollinator Meadow! Bring warm drinks to cheers and celebr
 ate as we complete a gentle path through the meadow. This is a great time 
 for volunteers to return to see how far the meadow has come.\n\nWork is st
 renuous to moderate. Ages 12 to 15 are welcome with a parent or guardian p
 resent. Ages 15 and above require a signature by a parent or guardian on a
  [liability waiver](https://1drv.ms/b/c/d5fb9d3835660a78/IQCJO4IIj6GnQ6N4R
 uNC981xAYL2kFajs9_RL8f8V7NkhaM?e=5bd5oi)\; teenagers cannot just be droppe
 d off.\n\nPlease arrive 5 to 10 minutes early so we can start promptly at 
 10 am.\n\nPlease dress appropriately! Wear long pants\, long-sleeved shirt
 \, closed-toe shoes or rain boots. Please no bug spray. We supply tools. I
 f you have gloves\, bring them or you can borrow a pair from us. Remember 
 to bring your own water!\n\nYou can download a copy of our [liability waiv
 er](https://1drv.ms/b/c/d5fb9d3835660a78/IQCJO4IIj6GnQ6N4RuNC981xAYL2kFajs
 9_RL8f8V7NkhaM?e=5bd5oi) to print\, sign and bring to the event.\n\nWe occ
 asionally use photos of events in promotional materials and social media. 
 By attending the event\, I consent to photos of me being used in promotion
 al materials or on social media.\n\nFor information\, contact program coor
 dinator Lori LaBorde at citizenscience@[somocon.org](http://somocon.org/)\
 n\n**Meet at the meadow after parking in Shady Nook Picnic Area.**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/317469626/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261117T160303Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261117T160303Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
